{
 "note": "The shops of the towns beyond the six old services (core/game/game_shops.gd, core/game/game_shop_stock.gd, checked by tools/check_data.gd). Each is a service a town lists in world.json, with a building behind a door (spaces.json `town_doors`, towns.json `sizes`, buildings.json art), a keeper (people.json, villagers.json) and a shelf of goods that is GENERATED, never listed: `stock` is a list of pools drawn from `items.json` by kinds, tags or ids (and `seasons`), from the loot generator (made-up gear), from the materials list and from the farm market, on dice keyed on the seed, the town, the shop and the year and season, so shelves differ between towns and change with the seasons and the dynasty's dice are untouched. `buys` is what the shop will buy (items by kind, tag or id; materials from the family's stores by id or tag; `all` for a pawnbroker) at `buy` of its value; `markup` is what it sells at over an item's price; `hours` are when it is open ([open, close] on the 24-hour clock); `tier_bonus` lets a rich shop stock items of a tier above the town's. None of these shops is a service the autopilot knows (GameItems.SHOPS is still the six), so autopilot lives are exactly what they were.",
